 {"id":"fabro-b1d3","title":"Slack: annotate bookkeeping-only runs in the run.completed payload","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-10T08:41:36.478Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T10:13:59.806Z","description":"When the run diff touches only .fabro/journal/** and .seeds/**, annotate the Slack run.completed payload (notifications settings or closeout emit site) as bookkeeping-only. Expected effect: humans can triage no-op runs in Slack instead of opening journal-only PRs. Grounded: run 01M256QJB48JK8BXJE1TVM2HYS's PR #115 contained only journal and tracker flips and was indistinguishable from a code PR in the Slack notification. Complements open seed fabro-9f97 (skip PR creation on journal-only diffs), which covers the PR side; this covers the notification side. Basis: run 01M256QJB48JK8BXJE1TVM2HYS, workflow version 38bab0b8b1faad62aaddb5e68facf6f1c58286169676479d3edbf99d4205b91c, commit 4d8a1e7f7a4fd74bed2dad41516106a8969a7e0b","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
